# Start copilot-alt.service when the internal keyboard appears: at every boot,
# when udev replays the devices the kernel found, and again whenever the kernel
# re-creates the device. That keyboard is the one on the i8042 controller,
# matched by the ID_PATH that bin/copilot-alt's by-path link is named after.
#
# The systemd tag is what makes systemd track the device, and only a device it
# tracks can want a unit. Not limited to "add": a "change" event that left the
# tag off would take it away again.
#
# Numbered after 60-persistent-input.rules, which sets ID_PATH, and
# 60-input-id.rules, which sets ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD. The remapper's own clone is
# a virtual device with no ID_PATH, so it never matches.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_PATH}=="platform-i8042-serio-0", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="copilot-alt.service"
